     continuation") certificates do NOT implement the note's F3 recursion:
     the code truncates psi to a ~2-cell band above the front (band top
     advancing at kernel speed from an empty start), whereas an admissible
     adversary can inject junk up to box width at ANY layer cell each row
     (u != w at a zero-load in-box cell), and such mass falls back onto the
     front pair at 1+delta offsets/row.  Re-running the chains with the
     note's own FULL-layer majorant: the seeded certificates STILL validate
     and STILL predict the death rows exactly, but first at rows 46/95
     (~0.09R), not 25/42 (~0.04R).  Consequence: G3's headline stands;
     the ledger's seeded validation rows, its "psi stays 3-8 bits below the
     pair" margins, and D3 sec. 5's "no-return window 2..21 rows after
     first-super" are band-truncation artifacts and must be restated from
     full-layer runs (no-return for the full T2-licensed class is certified
     from ~0.09R at these scales; the NI-class rows are as published).
   - L*(d) - ceil(2d/3) in {0,1}: CONFIRMED at 7 degrees to d = 2538.
   - The G3-precondition margin table (order parameter m/Theta') and the
     6/6 + 5/5 ledger counts: schema-checked; (512,4) state at row 15
     (d=319, L=213, gap=106, m_bits=theta_bits=292) reproduced exactly.

